--
N5008 [temp.param]/18: a template parameter pack of a FUNCTION template may be
followed by further template parameters that have a default argument (or
are deducible); [temp.variadic]/1: the pack accepts zero or more template
arguments, so every explicitly specified argument from the pack's position
on belongs to the pack ([temp.arg.explicit]/9) and the following
parameters take their defaults.  The explicit-argument check assumed a pack
is the last parameter and matched `char' in `get<int, char>()' against the
non-type parameter F ("found no match for symbol 'get'").  libc++'s
`__get_comp_type<_Ts...>()' (template <class... _Ts, bool _False = false>)
behind common_comparison_category_t (KNOWNBUG
cpp20_compare_three_way_pointers_libcxx).  Fixed in round 163b.
Out of scope: extending such a pack by deduction after explicit arguments
(`sum<int>(1, 2)' with `template <class... Ts, int N = 7> int sum(Ts...)')
still fails, as it did before.
